 "sources": [
  {
   "title": "open-audiovisual generic layout",
   "note": "No single fixture behind it: a common channel order, written by hand. Read the manual of your light and, where its order or ranges differ, copy this file and change it before patching a real fixture. The strobe ranges say open and strobe but no Hz: a generic file cannot know how fast a given value flashes, so under the 3 Hz cap the engine keeps this channel open. Pan and tilt start at the middle (128). Which value of reset moves the head back home, and what the built-in programs do, differs from fixture to fixture: program and reset are control channels, written only by an explicit call (a built-in program flashes as it likes, outside the cap)."
  }
 ],
